  "id": "predictive-validity",
  "term": "predictive validity",
  "definition": "Predictive validity is the extent to which a measure taken earlier can accurately forecast a later outcome. In this context, it refers to how well early or mid-year literacy assessments predict students’ end-of-year word reading fluency and help identify those at risk for reading difficulties.",
